# What `COPY . .` should not ship.
#
# There was no .dockerignore at all, so the build context was the whole working
# tree — including `.git`, every `__pycache__`, and the pytest caches. On the
# VPS that `COPY` step measured 61.7s. The context is only about 19MB, so this
# is a slow disk rather than a big tree, which is exactly the case where not
# copying something is the only way to make it faster.
#
# Tests stay available to the development target. The production target copies
# only runtime directories and does not install test dependencies.

.git
.gitignore
.github

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Local virtualenvs, if anyone keeps one in the tree.
.venv*/
venv/
node_modules/
.claude/
.codex/
.agents/

# Never bake secrets into an image. The compose files pass the real one in
# with `env_file:` at run time; `.env.example` stays, it is documentation.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
source-intake-*.txt

# Generated documents and backups live on the `storage_data` volume.
storage/

docs/
ROADMAP.md
